      "created_at": "2018-12-31T05:41:27Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-12-31T05:41:27Z",
      "body": "I'd argue it's never a good idea to be saving things to localStorage without the author specifically intending to. It just seems like odd behavior for a generic WYSIWYG editor. I don't believe the regular Trix library does this. Additionally, some countries around the world have very strict privacy laws in regard to cookies, etc. \r\n\r\nWhy not at least create an option for turning it off? I'd argue to have it off by default, but that's just my opinion. Thanks for considering this request. Have a good day!",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
